            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0824" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Grew) to the Acting Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-10T20:00:00+09:00">June 10, 1933—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 10—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. Department’s 56, June 9, 6 p.m. The Department’s instructions were carried
                    out this afternoon. The Foreign Office states that the Japanese Army authorities
                    in Manchuria are already doing their best to effect the release of Nielsen but
                    that the desire of the United States Government as expressed by the Department
                    will be conveyed to them immediately. The Foreign Office assured the Embassy
                    that everything possible would be done.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
